{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe remote gate is refs/reconciler/gate. Older binaries require a non-empty gated_mode string and fail closed on unkn...\nThere is no duration or automatic expiry. An --until field would diverge old and new readers and could silently unpau...\nThe existing set_gate and clear_gate ref writers already use expected-old-oid CAS. Pause and resume preserve that mec...\nPause provenance is deterministic. who is the repository git config user.email resolved by git config --get user.emai...\nA live error-path bug crosses the same seam: check_phase_gate runs before the reconciler try block today, so a corrup...\n## Operator and workflow behavior\n- rebar bridge pause REASON requires a nonblank reason and writes the additive dual-format blob.\n- Pausing an already-paused bridge is idempotent only when the requested reason matches; it reports the existing paus...\n- rebar bridge resume clears the gate through the same CAS seam. Resuming an unpaused bridge exits 0 with a notice.\n- Missing origin refuses loudly; CAS conflict exits nonzero with the re-read remote state; corrupt state exits 1 with...\n- A new paused gate blocks mutating reconciler modes as a benign exit 0 and emits exactly one stderr line: BRIDGE_PAU...\n- .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml preserves every existing rc mapping. On rc 0 it captures and replays reconci...\n## Compatibility and test plan\nUse expand-contract ordering: additive reader and dual-format writer ship together. Feed every new blob to a vendored...\nSurface parity census:\n- CLI command: in scope through real rebar bridge pause/resume subprocess tests.\n- MCP or API tool: out of scope because pause/resume are intentionally operator-only writes in this story; the persis...\n- Library facade: out of scope for the same operator-only boundary; existing reconcile library behavior is unchanged.\n- Automated callers: in scope through the scheduled workflow contract and real legacy reconcile entrypoint.\n- Dual direction: in scope; pause writes and blocks, resume clears and restores mutation, with exact remote state ass...\nNo new contention harness is needed: each operator action is one existing expected-old-oid CAS operation, not a compo...\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every new gate blob carries paused, reason, who, paused_at and retains gated_mode: reconcile-check.\n- [ ] who is repository git user.email; missing identity refuses without a write; paused_at is first-pause UTC RFC333...\n- [ ] A vendored pre-change decoder accepts every blob the new writer emits, and real legacy reconcile coverage prove...\n- [ ] rebar bridge pause REASON and rebar bridge resume are the only new supported write path; old reconcile vocabula...\n- [ ] Blank reasons are rejected; same-reason re-pause is idempotent without metadata loss; different-reason re-pause...\n- [ ] Existing expected-old-oid CAS protects pause/resume, and a conflict surfaces current remote state without blind...\n- [ ] A genuine new pause blocks mutating bridge work with exit 0 and the exact single-line BRIDGE_PAUSED JSON marker...\n- [ ] Pause detects a missing remote and refuses rather than reporting local-only success.\n- [ ] The scheduled workflow notices only the BRIDGE_PAUSED: rc-0 outcome and preserves ordinary success, legacy beni...\n- [ ] No --until, automatic expiry, new-only blob value, check_phase_gate rename, or old-vocabulary removal ships.\n[full output: \"$HOME/Library/Application Support/rtk/tee/1786208194_jq_-r__description___gsub__emits_one_sta.log\"]"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786208194996898001,"uuid":"e26b50f8-8445-45d1-a590-c8138c2cadbf"}